    {'para': '**244.** In a few roots, when a final sonant aspirate (⟨gh⟩, ⟨dh⟩, ⟨bh⟩; also ⟨h⟩, representing ⟨gh⟩) loses its aspiration according to §§ 239. 3, 242, the initial sonant consonant (⟨g⟩, ⟨d⟩, or ⟨b⟩) becomes aspirate; thus, ⟨budh⟩, nom.-voc. sing. ⟨bhut⟩; ⟨bhudbhis⟩, ⟨bhutsu⟩.'},
    {'para': '**245. Agreement of adjectives.** If the same adjective qualify two or more substantives, it will be used in their combined number; if the substantives are masculine and feminine, the adj. will be masc.; but in a combination of masc. or fem. subjects with neuter, the adjective will be neuter.'},
